# A clause set with one seeded inconsistency.
#
# Two unit clauses assert `p(a)` and its negation, which `mm-cli verify run symbolic`
# refutes by unit resolution. The gate line is:
#
#     mm-cli verify run symbolic --subject bench/tools/seeded_inconsistency.logic ; test $? -ne 0
#
# The refutation is sound — it can only fire when the two literals really are
# complementary — and the check is deliberately incomplete in the other direction: a set
# it cannot refute is reported `inconclusive`, never `proven`. That is what makes this
# fixture a test of the verifier rather than a test of a grep.

p(a)
not p(a)
